# Copy to .env.local. Both values come from your Supabase project:
# Project Settings → API.
#
# With these unset the app runs against this device's own localStorage — no
# invented data, just an empty install that /start can provision a company
# into. With them set, every read and write goes to Postgres instead and
# row-level security decides what each signed-in person may see.
#
# Before setting them, apply supabase/migrations/ to the project and make sure
# an OTP channel is configured under Authentication → Providers: sign-in sends
# a one-time code, and with no channel enabled nobody can get in.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://fdxwxcwnzzcsnsxdhzjj.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon public key>
